<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Solador per-host metrics agent: the macOS LaunchAgent (#392).

  Generated by deploy/install.sh from agent/deploy/app.solador.agent.plist,
  whose at-sign placeholders it renders (XML-escaped) into the paths it
  actually installed to; a re-run regenerates this file. It is bootstrapped
  into the invoking user's gui/<uid> domain. A LaunchAgent, not a
  LaunchDaemon: it runs as the user who installed it, never as root, and it
  starts at that user's login rather than at boot. A host that nobody logs in
  to does not run this agent — say so rather than pretend otherwise.

  ProgramArguments is the launcher, then the binary, the env file and the log
  file — every path the launcher needs arrives here, so it does not assume
  launchd's HOME is the installer's; it reads $HOME only to extend PATH for
  the container CLIs that no-admin installs put under the home directory. The
  bearer token is NOT here: launchd's EnvironmentVariables would put it into a
  world-readable plist, so the launcher reads ~/.config/solador-agent.env
  (mode 0600) at every start instead, and rotating the token stays "edit that
  file, restart the service" on both platforms.

  PATH, on the other hand, IS set here, and it is load-bearing. launchd starts
  a job with its compiled-in PATH (/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin), which holds
  none of docker (/usr/local/bin), tart (/opt/homebrew/bin) or podman
  (/opt/podman/bin); the agent maps a runtime it cannot find to "not
  installed" and serves /v1/containers as [] forever while /v1/health stays
  green — the empty-panel-as-all-clear failure this project exists to avoid.
  systemd's user session inherits a PATH that already includes /usr/local/bin,
  which is why the Linux unit needs no counterpart. PATH is not a secret, so
  the argument against EnvironmentVariables above does not apply to it.

  KeepAlive + RunAtLoad is systemd's Restart=always; the throttle is launchd's
  RestartSec. No ProcessType: "Background" would put the 1 Hz sampler in the
  background QoS tier, whose timer coalescing (tens of ms of leeway) skews the
  disk/network rates that divide by a nominal interval, exactly when the host
  is busy. The Linux unit sets no Nice= either.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>@LABEL@</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>@LAUNCHER@</string>
        <string>@BINARY@</string>
        <string>@ENV_FILE@</string>
        <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/podman/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>3</integer>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>@LOG_FILE@</string>
</dict>
</plist>
